#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:409
msgid "Exercise 6: Aligning conformations to a template"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:411
msgid ""
"In this exercise, we will learn how to align a MD trajectory to a reference "
"conformation, after fixing possible discontinuities due to PBCs. The goal is"
" to compute the vertical position of the serotonin ligand with respect to "
"the lipid bilayer. In the simulations of membrane proteins, typically the "
"initial conformation is oriented so that the lipid bilayer is parallel to "
"the xy plane (look for example at `5-HT1B.pdb`). Therefore, initially one "
"could use for example the coordinate `z` of the geometric center of the "
"ligand to measure how far it is from the membrane bilayer. However, during "
"the simulation:"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:413
msgid "the system can translate from its original position;"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:414
msgid "the system can be broken by PBCs;"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:416
msgid ""
"therefore one could not use an absolute position to keep track of the "
"location of the ligand. To solve this problem, there are several PLUMED "
"actions that can be used to make sure the system is not broken by PBCs, to "
"re-align it to a reference conformation, and thus to use absolute positions "
"safely."
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:418
msgid ""
"To complete this exercise, the users will need to make heavy use of the "
"PLUMED [manual](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-"
"doc/html/colvarintro.html) to prepare the input file on their own. In the "
"following, some suggestions will be given:"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:420
msgid ""
"first, make sure the entire protein is not broken by PBCs using "
"WHOLEMOLECULES;"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:421
msgid ""
"then, make sure the ligand is not broken by PBCs and in the same cell as the"
" protein, using the WRAPAROUND action and the `GROUPBY` option;"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:422
msgid ""
"to align the _stable_ protein residues (as defined in exercise 5 above, i.e."
" residues 41 to 390) to the template `5-HT1B.pdb`, you can use "
"FIT_TO_TEMPLATE;"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:423
msgid ""
"at this point, you can safely define the position of the geometric center of"
" the ligand using the POSITION CV with the option `NOPBC`;"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:424
msgid "the requested CV is the `z` component of the POSITION CV."
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:426
msgid ""
"You can check that your PLUMED input file is correct in two ways. First, you"
" can print out the conformations of the system after the transformations "
"done by WHOLEMOLECULES, WRAPAROUND, and FIT_TO_TEMPLATE by modifying your "
"input file as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:439
msgid ""
"Now, you can visualize the `5-HT1B_aligned.gro` file using "
"[VMD](https://www.ks.uiuc.edu/Research/vmd/). Second, if you inspect the "
"time series of your CV, this should be a continuous trajectory that spans "
"the range from 9 nm to 18 nm."
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:441
msgid "Exercise 7: Estimating binding propensity"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:443
msgid ""
"In this last exercise, we want to determine the propensity of the serotonin "
"ligand to bind the first 40 N-terminal flexible residues of the 5-HT1B "
"receptor and if there are hot-spots where binding is more favorite. In order"
" to answer to these questions, the user will:"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:445
msgid ""
"compute the fraction of bound conformations over the total number of frames "
"in the MD trajectory;"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:446
msgid ""
"for each individual residue and glycan, compute the fraction of bound "
"conformation per residue/glycan;"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:447
msgid ""
"dump all bound conformations to a `gro` file, after fixing PBCs as in "
"exercise 6 above;"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:448
msgid ""
"for each individual residue and glycan, dump all bound conformations to a "
"separate `gro` file, after fixing PBCs."
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:450
msgid ""
"To solve this exercise, no template PLUMED input file nor any indication of "
"the procedure to follow will be given. The users should only keep in mind "
"that:"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:452
msgid ""
"we arbitrarily define as *bound* a conformation in which at least one pair "
"of atoms of the ligand and of the protein/residue/glycan is closer than 0.4 "
"nm;"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:453
msgid ""
"any pre-exisiting CV defined in the PLUMED "
"[manual](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-doc/html/colvarintro.html) can"
" be used;"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:454
msgid ""
"any CV defined directly by the user in the PLUMED input file via the CUSTOM "
"action can be used."
msgstr ""
